From: Jay Leaton <contact@buildthings.co>
Date: Sat, 03 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Spark stack for TensorFold 0.6.0: the GLM-5.3-Flash
 two-DGX-Spark engine

families/glm5_next/spark/ (TF_GLM_ENGINE=spark): TensorFold 0.3.4's GLM CUDA engine with the
glm53-tensorfold-spark patch series (0001-0620) rebased onto 0.6.0, plus the CUDA communicator
interface (cuda/comm.py: transports that wrap NCCL, byte gathers, two-rank swaps), a family
CUDA_SERVE hook, and a server fix for sockets past descriptor 1023.

The DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash family builds on this tree: it reuses the RoCE all-gather, the
communicator and the server. The shipped GLM draft-vocabulary ranking is the public-text one
of glm53-tensorfold-spark (patches/0420, bench/draftvocab_public.py).
