@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# GLM-5.3-Flash on two DGX Sparks at 1M tokens (the Spark engine)
+
+`TF_GLM_ENGINE=spark` on both ranks serves GLM-5.3-Flash through `glm5_next/spark/` instead of
+`glm5_next/cuda/`. It is the engine behind a two-Spark deployment that serves four concurrent requests of up
+to 1,048,576 tokens each (prompt plus reply) from the EXL3 checkpoint
+`neko-legends/GLM-5.3-Flash-Uncensored-EXL3` and the optional DFlash2 drafter.
+
+```bash
+TF_GLM_ENGINE=spark GLM53_TF_LATENT_KV=1 GLM53_TF_KV_DTYPE=fp8 GLM53_TF_BATCH=4 GLM53_TF_KV_POOL_TOKENS=1048576 \
+  tensorfold serve MODEL --tp 2 --rank 1 --master 192.0.2.1 --context 1048576
+TF_GLM_ENGINE=spark ... tensorfold serve MODEL --tp 2 --rank 0 --master 192.0.2.1 --context 1048576 --name glm
+```
+
+Both ranks need the same `TF_GLM_ENGINE` and the same `GLM53_TF_*` settings; the engine checks the ones that
+change the collective sequence at load. The speed and memory knobs default to the 0.3.4 engine's behaviour
+(the defaults that are on, such as the client-disconnect check, change no reply). The tested production set is
+the deployment's `prod.env`.
+
+## What it adds
+
+| Area | Knobs (`GLM53_TF_*`) | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Weights | `NONEXPERT=q4mse`, `EXPERT_LOOP`, `PREPARED` | non-expert weights in 4 bits (MSE-clipped), expert loops, prepared per-rank folders for 10-40 s restarts |
+| KV cache | `LATENT_KV=1`, `KV_DTYPE=fp8`, `KV_POOL_TOKENS` | latent MLA rows (512 wide), FP8 rows with a power-of-two scale (7.4 KB a token a rank), one paged pool shared by the request slots |
+| Long context | `SELECT`, `INDEX_RING`, `SELECT_SCRATCH` | indexer rings and blocked top-k selection for 1M tokens, selection scratch that grows as needed |
+| Prefill | `FAST_PREFILL`, `LEAN_PREFILL`, `PREFILL_OVERLAP`, `PREFILL_PP`, `B12X=4`, `MOE_GLUE`, `ATTN_BM32`, `MLA_EXPAND=v2` | chunk-grid prefill whose state is independent of the chunk size, pipelined all-gathers, row-split hyper-connections, one-pass sparse latent attention |
+| Decode | `DEC_EXPERT_LOADS`, `L2PF`, `DECODE_OVERLAP`, `MAX_DRAFT_ROWS` | routed-expert load path, L2 prefetch of the next weights, host work off the critical path, verify windows of up to 16 rows |
+| Drafting | `CALIB`, `DEPTH=cost`, `LOOKUP`, `AUTO_FDRAFTS` | measured round costs, cost-derived draft depths, prompt-lookup drafts beside MTP and DFlash2 |
+| Requests | `BATCH=4`, `BATCH_*`, `SOLO_PIECE`, `MULTI_PREFILL` | four request slots sharing rounds, one forward for a round's prefill pieces |
+| Sessions | `SESSION_GIB`, `SESSION_DISK`, `PREFIX_SHARE`, `SNAPSHOT_BEFORE_END` | conversation snapshots in RAM and on NVMe, shared system prompts, a warm replay of an identical prompt |
+| Comm | `COMM_BACKEND=roce`, `ROCE_*` | one-shot RoCE all-gathers of up to 256 KiB over both CX7 functions, NCCL fallback with a failure marker |
+| Server | `VISION`, `GRAMMAR`, `TOOL_FIXES`, `REASONING_FIELDS`, `DEFAULT_EFFORT`, `REQUEST_LOG`, `DISCONNECT` | images, structured output under drafting and batching, tool-call fixes, OpenAI-shaped context errors, `/metrics`, `/tokenize` |
+
+Measured options that are not part of the production set (`FAST_EXPERTS=tc|fat2|auto`, `KDA_V2`, `SPARSE_V2`,
+`DRAFT_VOCAB`, `GPU_ROUND`, `NONEXPERT=q8`, `DEC_QMM_MAXMB`, `BATCH_ADAPT`, `BATCH_BUCKETS`) stay off by default.
+
+## Exactness
+
+The contract is the family's: a drafted reply equals its `"draft": false` reply, a request in a four-slot round
+equals itself alone, and a resumed request equals a fresh one. The engine keeps 0.3.4's weight layout and
+arithmetic, so its replies are bit-identical to the same engine on 0.3.4 for the same knobs.
+
+## Relation to `glm5_next/cuda`
+
+`glm5_next/cuda` (the default) is TensorFold's own GLM engine: shared 4-bit lane matmuls, its latent cache and
+startup admission, one request at a time. The Spark engine has its own admission (the pool and slot rule), its
+own session store in place of the kept prompts, and its own server (`spark/server.py`, served through the
+family's `CUDA_SERVE`). Prepared folders keep the key and class names they had on the 0.3.4 layout
+(`fastboot.KEY_PKG`), so both layouts read the same folders.
+
+## Licence
+
+TensorFold is Apache-2.0 from 0.6.0. The Spark engine is code written before 0.6.0 (0.3.4's GLM engine and the
+glm53-tensorfold-spark patches on it), so it keeps the MIT notice in `LICENSES/MIT.txt`; THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
+lists its sources (b12x, Apache-2.0; the fat-expert kit, Apache-2.0 / MIT).
